## Why `curl_cffi`, `requests`, and `fetch` were chosen

| Library | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| **`curl_cffi`** | TLS fingerprint mimicry (avoids Cloudflare blocks). Used by `deepcli` for API calls. |
| **`requests`** | Simpler cookie handling. We used it for tests because `curl_cffi`’s cookie jar doesn’t merge the same way. |
| **`fetch` (Node)** | Deepterm’s approach. Sends cookies natively (`credentials: "include"`), exactly like a browser. |

The orchestrator uses `curl_cffi` because it needs to evade bot detection. For Account 2 to work with the orchestrator, we need Account 2’s **own Bearer token** — which the above steps will produce.

